# Frontend configuration. Server-side secrets still live in trip-planner-api.
VITE_TRIP_PLANNER_API_URL=http://localhost:4300

# NOT a real secret — Vite inlines this into the public JS bundle. It's a
# filter against scripted abuse of trip-planner-api, not access control; see
# src/lib/api.ts. Must match trip-planner-api's FRONTEND_API_SECRET exactly.
# Falls back to trip-planner-api's own local-dev default if unset.
VITE_TRIP_PLANNER_API_SECRET=local-dev-frontend-secret

# Google Street View Static API key, for the photo previews that open on a
# map pin (see src/lib/streetImagery.ts). Vite inlines this into the public
# JS bundle, so it is NOT protected by being here - lock it down in Google
# Cloud Console before deploying:
#   * Application restriction: HTTP referrers, listing only your UI origins.
#   * API restriction: Street View Static API only (nothing else).
# Billing note: opening one pin costs 4 image requests (four headings from
# the same panorama); the free metadata probe that precedes them is not
# billed. Leave this empty and the pin popup simply says previews are not
# configured instead of breaking.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
